5. app/page.tsx — 'use client'. The orchestrator. On mount, GET /api/patients. Left column = PatientPicker + an optional collapsible "Paste raw notes instead" textarea (with a "reason for visit" input). A primary "Generate briefing" button. On click POST /api/prep. While loading show a skeleton version of BriefingView in the right column. On success show BriefingView. On error show an inline error card. Include a small persistent disclaimer line: "Prep aid for a licensed clinician. Not diagnosis or treatment advice. Verify against the chart." Include the product name "Clinic Prep Assistant" and a one-line tagline in a header with the gradient glow behind it.

TYPES (mirror these EXACTLY — define a local `types.ts` under components/ or inline; do NOT import from lib/):
  type Priority = 'high' | 'med' | 'low';
  type FlagCategory = 'safety' | 'missing-info' | 'contradiction' | 'stale';
  type Briefing = {
    summary: { oneLiner: string; activeProblems: string[]; medications: string[]; allergies: string[]; recentChanges: string[] };
    followUpQuestions: { question: string; why: string; priority: Priority }[];
    flags: { category: FlagCategory; message: string; evidence: string }[];
    briefingMarkdown: string;
  };
  type PatientListItem = { id: string; name: string; age: number; sex: string; reason: string };

API CONTRACT (already frozen — code against it):
- GET /api/patients → 200 { patients: PatientListItem[] }
- POST /api/prep → request body { patientId: string } OR { notes: string, reason?: string, patientName?: string }
    → 200 { briefing: Briefing, patient: { name: string; age?: number; sex?: string } }
    → on failure: non-2xx with { error: string }

Render the STRUCTURED briefing fields (do NOT add a markdown-rendering library; briefingMarkdown is only used for the Copy button). Use only `react` and Tailwind. Keep components small and clean. Make it look genuinely premium — this is being demoed. When done, reply with the list of files you created and any assumptions.

